THESIS

The strongest opportunity is not =E2=80=9Canother mining calculator.=E2=80=
=9D The
emerging market is physical compute capital: CPUs, GPUs and ASICs
whose value depends on mining yield, resale value, electricity cost,
rental yield, depreciation and workload optionality.

Core framing:

POW =3D the economic graph of physical computation.

A Compute Asset is any physical device capable of transforming
electricity into economically valuable computation.

ComputeAsset
=E2=86=92 purchase / resale market
=E2=86=92 physical characteristics
=E2=86=92 possible workloads
   =E2=80=A2 BTC mining
   =E2=80=A2 XMR mining
   =E2=80=A2 QUBIC mining
   =E2=80=A2 other PoW
   =E2=80=A2 AI inference
   =E2=80=A2 AI training
   =E2=80=A2 rendering
   =E2=80=A2 cloud rental
   =E2=80=A2 idle/resale
=E2=86=92 location-specific power + hosting
=E2=86=92 expected cashflows
=E2=86=92 fair asset value

The user-facing questions become:
1. What should this physical unit of compute be doing right now?
2. What physical compute should I buy given every workload it could
perform over its life?

MARKET CONFIRMATION

The market is already being financialized, but in silos.

Luxor reports $865M+ of hardware transacted from 2022=E2=80=932025 across
ASICs, GPUs and CPUs, with shipments to 36 countries. Its business now
spans hardware brokerage, mining pools, firmware, energy optimization
and hashrate derivatives.

Luxor has also built a hashrate derivatives market with >$500M OTC
volume, allowing miners to trade future compute revenue.

Hashrate Index launched an AI Hardware Price Index in August 2026
specifically because secondary-market AI hardware pricing remains
opaque. This is strong evidence that compute hardware itself is
becoming a financial asset class.

Sources:
