CORE POW DERIVED METRICS

1. Compute Asset Yield (CAY)

CAY =3D
annualized best-use net cashflow
/
asset acquisition price

A cap rate for compute hardware.

2. PoW Acquisition Spread (PAS)

For Qubic:

PAS =3D
QUBIC mined per $
/
QUBIC bought spot per $

PAS > 1 =3D> mining acquires QUBIC cheaper than spot.
PAS < 1 =3D> buying QUBIC dominates.

3. Compute Optionality (CO)

Value machines that can switch across multiple economically
independent workloads.

CO =E2=89=88 sum(P_i =C3=97 Y_i) - switching costs

4. Liquidation-adjusted yield (LRY)

LRY =3D
Revenue
- Energy
- Depreciation

This prevents false =E2=80=9Cprofitability=E2=80=9D from ignoring collapsin=
g hardware
resale value.

5. Buy-vs-Rent spread

BR =3D
annualized rental-equivalent revenue
/
hardware purchase price

Highlights hardware cheap relative to cloud pricing.

6. Mining Premium

MP =3D
hardware market price
-
fair value from non-mining uses

Useful for identifying speculative hardware bubbles.

7. Scarcity Index

Combine:
inventory =E2=86=93
price =E2=86=91
time-to-sale =E2=86=93
rental price =E2=86=91
utilization =E2=86=91

into one hardware scarcity signal.

